From 319af32d700654962dd0201649e93d8c933ed0a3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: stevedamnvan <100538383+stevedamnvan@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 02:36:07 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] GC-ASSET r17 (gate-ON only): kind check per consumer,
 member-selected replay keeps a held serial; host tests repaired

- gc_asset_gate.cpp emitted_checked: a token counts only for its own kind (a motion row only for Motion, any other
  row never for Motion), first sight or seen; else why=kind-mismatch.
- native_model.cpp: a deferred replay of a part selected through its model member (gc-catalog24b) keeps the queued
  serial only when member_contains(serial, drawn BIN, 64); otherwise 0 as before (h2: the 2 not-covered
  unbound-accepted-model after the codec screen, replay serial 0x27, payload none).
- gc_asset_members.cpp: weak ensure_disc_catalog (false) so host builds without gc_asset_disc.cpp link.
- tests: test_gate kind-mismatch cases; test_runtime_index expects the mismatch; test_runtime_hooks replay keep
  case; fixtures take the PROF probe globals, StdRoom.gca_unused and the world seal stubs; actor_main mutant
  'restore positive replay' retired (24b member acceptance). C++ host tests PASS; python 43 -> 16 failing.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01AkGpf8W8oYKd2z6cLgVseU
